 WordPress file and folder permission settings govern the accessibility and read/write privileges of the files and folders which make up your WP installation.'=>'Your WordPress file and folder permission settings govern the accessibility and read/write privileges of the files and folders which make up your WP installation.','File permissions scan'=>'File permissions scan','Unable to change permissions for %s'=>'Unable to change permissions for %s','The permissions for %s were successfully changed to %s'=>'The permissions for %s were successfully changed to %s','Host system logs'=>'Host system logs','PHP file editing'=>'PHP file editing','The following files were changed on your website.'=>'The following files were changed on your website.','The following files were removed from your website.'=>'The following files were removed from your website.','File modified'=>'File modified','File size'=>'File size','The following files were added to your website.'=>'The following files were added to your website.','Latest file change scan results'=>'Latest file change scan results','No contract (cancel anytime)'=>'No contract (cancel anytime)','404 event logs'=>'404 event logs','A locked visitor will be automatically redirected to this URL.'=>'A locked visitor will be automatically redirected to this URL.','404 lockout redirect URL'=>'404 lockout redirect URL','Set the length of time for which a locked IP address will be prevented from visiting your site.'=>'Set the length of time for which a locked IP address will be prevented from visiting your site.','Time length of 404 lockout (minutes)'=>'Time length of 404 lockout (minutes)','Check this if you want to enable the logging of 404 events'=>'Check this if you want to enable the logging of 404 events','Enable 404 event logging'=>'Enable 404 event logging','404 detection options'=>'404 detection options','Such behaviour can mean that a hacker might be trying to find a particular page or URL for sinister reasons.'=>'Such behaviour can mean that a hacker might be trying to find a particular page or URL for sinister reasons.','However, in some cases you may find many repeated 404 errors which occur in a relatively short space of time and from the same IP address which are all attempting to access a variety of non-existent page URLs.'=>'However, in some cases you may find many repeated 404 errors which occur in a relatively short space of time and from the same IP address which are all attempting to access a variety of non-existent page URLs.','Typically, most 404 errors happen quite innocently when people have mistyped a URL or used an old link to page which doesn\'t exist anymore.'=>'Typically, most 404 errors happen quite innocently when people have mistyped a URL or used an old link to page which doesn\'t exist anymore.','A 404 or Not Found error occurs when somebody tries to access a non-existent page on your website.'=>'A 404 or Not Found error occurs when somebody tries to access a non-existent page on your website.','404 detection configuration'=>'404 detection configuration','All 404 event logs were deleted from the database successfully.'=>'All 404 event logs were deleted from the database successfully.','Prevent hotlinking'=>'Prevent hotlinking','This feature will prevent people from directly hotlinking images from your site\'s pages by writing some directives in your .htaccess file.'=>'This feature will prevent people from directly hotlinking images from your site\'s pages by writing some directives in your .htaccess file.','Due to the fact that the image being displayed on the other person\'s site is coming from your server, this can cause leaking of bandwidth and resources for you because your server has to present this image for the people viewing it on someone elses\'s site.'=>'Due to the fact that the image being displayed on the other person\'s site is coming from your server, this can cause leaking of bandwidth and resources for you because your server has to present this image for the people viewing it on someone elses\'s site.','A hotlink is where someone displays an image on their site which is actually located on your site by using a direct link to the source of the image on your server.'=>'A hotlink is where someone displays an image on their site which is actually located on your site by using a direct link to the source of the image on your server.','Prevent image hotlinking'=>'Prevent image hotlinking','If the bot fails the checks then the plugin will mark it as being a fake Googlebot and it will block it'=>'If the bot fails the checks then the plugin will mark it as being a fake Googlebot and it will block it','It will then perform a few tests to verify if the bot is legitimately from Google and if so it will allow the bot to proceed.'=>'It will then perform a few tests to verify if the bot is legitimately from Google and if so it will allow the bot to proceed.','This feature will check if the User Agent information of a bot contains the string "Googlebot".'=>'This feature will check if the User Agent information of a bot contains the string "Googlebot".','Enable this if you want to block all fake Googlebots.'=>'Enable this if you want to block all fake Googlebots.','Block fake Googlebots'=>'Block fake Googlebots','Just be aware that if you activate this feature the plugin will block all bots which use the "Googlebot" string in their User Agent information but are NOT officially from Google (irrespective of whether they are malicious or not).'=>'Just be aware that if you activate this feature the plugin will block all bots which use the "Googlebot" string in their User Agent information but are NOT officially from Google (irrespective of whether they are malicious or not).','Googlebots have a unique identity which cannot easily be forged and this feature will identify any fake Google bots and block them from reading your site\'s pages.'=>'Googlebots have a unique identity which cannot easily be forged and this feature will identify any fake Google bots and block them from reading your site\'s pages.','This feature allows you to block bots which are impersonating as a Googlebot but actually aren\'t. (In other words they are fake Google bots)'=>'This feature allows you to block bots which are impersonating as a Googlebot but actually aren\'t. (In other words they are fake Google bots)','Although most of the bots out there are relatively harmless sometimes website owners want to have more control over which bots they allow into their site.'=>'Although most of the bots out there are relatively harmless sometimes website owners want to have more control over which bots they allow into their site.','A lot of bots are legitimate and non-malicious but not all bots are good and often you will find some which try to impersonate legitimate bots such as "Googlebot" but in reality they have nohing to do with Google at all.'=>'A lot of bots are legitimate and non-malicious but not all bots are good and often you will find some which try to impersonate legitimate bots such as "Googlebot" but in reality they have nohing to do with Google at all.','%s?'=>'%s?','What is an Internet Bot'=>'What is an Internet Bot','Internet bot settings'=>'Internet bot settings','Save 5G firewall settings'=>'Save 5G firewall settings','This setting will implement the 5G security firewall protection mechanisms on your site which include the following things:'=>'This setting will implement the 5G security firewall protection mechanisms on your site which include the following things:','Enable this to apply the 5G firewall protection from perishablepress.com to your site.'=>'Enable this to apply the 5G firewall protection from perishablepress.com to your site.','Enable legacy 5G firewall protection'=>'Enable legacy 5G firewall protection','....and much more.'=>'....and much more.','4) Stop attackers from manipulating query strings by disallowing illicit characters.'=>'4) Stop attackers from manipulating query strings by disallowing illicit characters.','3) Guard against the common patterns and specific exploits in the root portion of targeted URLs.'=>'3) Guard against the common patterns and specific exploits in the root portion of targeted URLs.','2) Block malicious encoded URL characters such as the ".css(" string.'=>'2) Block malicious encoded URL characters such as the ".css(" string.','1) Block forbidden characters commonly used in exploitative attacks.'=>'1) Block forbidden characters commonly used in exploitative attacks.','This setting will implement the 6G security firewall protection mechanisms on your site which include the following things:'=>'This setting will implement the 6G security firewall protection mechanisms on your site which include the following things:','Enable 6G firewall protection'=>'Enable 6G firewall protection','The 6G firewall is a simple, flexible blacklist that helps reduce the number of malicious URL requests that hit your website.'=>'The 6G firewall is a simple, flexible blacklist that helps reduce the number of malicious URL requests that hit your website.','This feature allows you to activate the %1$s (or legacy %2$s) firewall security protection rules designed and produced by %3$s.'=>'This feature allows you to activate the %1$s (or legacy %2$s) firewall security protection rules designed and produced by %3$s.','NOTE: Some strings for this setting might break some functionality.'=>'NOTE: Some strings for this setting might break some functionality.','This setting matches for common malicious string patterns and exploits and will produce a 403 error for the hacker attempting the query.'=>'This setting matches for common malicious string patterns and exploits and will produce a 403 error for the hacker attempting the query.','This is an advanced character string filter to prevent malicious string attacks on your site coming from Cross Site Scripting (XSS).'=>'This is an advanced character string filter to prevent malicious string attacks on your site coming from Cross Site Scripting (XSS).','Enable advanced character string filter'=>'Enable advanced character string filter','Enable this if you want this plugin to automatically block IP addresses which submit spam comments.'=>'Enable this if you want this plugin to automatically block IP addresses which submit spam comments.','Enable auto block of spam comment IPs'=>'Enable auto block of spam comment IPs','All time total:'=>'All time total:','Spammer IPs added to permanent block list today:'=>'Spammer IPs added to permanent block list today:','You currently have no IP addresses permanently blocked due to spam.'=>'You currently have no IP addresses permanently blocked due to spam.','This feature allows you to automatically and permanently block IP addresses which have exceeded a certain number of spam comments.'=>'This feature allows you to automatically and permanently block IP addresses which have exceeded a certain number of spam comments.','You entered a non-numeric value for the minimum spam comments per IP field; it has been set to the default value.'=>'You entered a non-numeric value for the minimum spam comments per IP field; it has been set to the default value.','You must enter an integer greater than zero for the minimum spam comments per IP field; it has been set to the default value.'=>'You must enter an integer greater than zero for the minimum spam comments per IP field; it has been set to the default value.','You entered a non-numeric value for the "minimum number of spam comments" field; it has been set to the default value.'=>'You entered a non-numeric value for the "minimum number of spam comments" field; it has been set to the default value.','A large portion of WordPress blog comment spam is produced by automated bots rather than by humans.'=>'A large portion of WordPress blog comment spam is produced by automated bots rather than by humans.','Enable this if you want to insert a CAPTCHA field on the comment forms.'=>'Enable this if you want to insert a CAPTCHA field on the comment forms.','Comment spam IP monitoring'=>'Comment spam IP monitoring','If your chosen server variable fails the plugin will automatically fall back to retrieving the IP address from $_SERVER["REMOTE_ADDR"]'=>'If your chosen server variable fails the plugin will automatically fall back to retrieving the IP address from $_SERVER["REMOTE_ADDR"]','Choose a $_SERVER variable you would like to detect visitors\' IP address using.'=>'Choose a $_SERVER variable you would like to detect visitors\' IP address using.','Select your import settings file'=>'Select your import settings file','Import AIOS settings'=>'Import AIOS settings','Export AIOS settings'=>'Export AIOS settings','For Example: If a settings item relies on the domain URL then it may not work correctly when imported into a site with a different domain.'=>'For Example: If a settings item relies on the domain URL then it may not work correctly when imported into a site with a different domain.','This can be handy if you wanted to save time by applying the settings from one site to another site.'=>'This can be handy if you wanted to save time by applying the settings from one site to another site.','This section allows you to export or import your All-In-One Security settings.'=>'This section allows you to export or import your All-In-One Security settings.','Export or import your AIOS settings'=>'Export or import your AIOS settings','The contents of your settings file are invalid, please check the contents of the file you are trying to import settings from.'=>'The contents of your settings file are invalid, please check the contents of the file you are trying to import settings from.','Please choose a file to import your settings from.'=>'Please choose a file to import your settings from.','Enable this if you want to remove the version and meta info produced by WP from all pages'=>'Enable this if you want to remove the version and meta info produced by WP from all pages','Remove WP generator meta info'=>'Remove WP generator meta info','WP generator meta info'=>'WP generator meta info','This feature will allow you to remove the WP generator meta info and other version info from your site\'s pages.'=>'This feature will allow you to remove the WP generator meta info and other version info from your site\'s pages.','The above meta information shows which version of WordPress your site is currently running and thus can help hackers or crawlers scan your site to see if you have an older version of WordPress or one with a known exploit.'=>'The above meta information shows which version of WordPress your site is currently running and thus can help hackers or crawlers scan your site to see if you have an older version of WordPress or one with a known exploit.','WordPress generator automatically adds some meta information inside the "head" tags of every page on your site\'s front end, below is an example of this:'=>'WordPress generator automatically adds some meta information inside the "head" tags of every page on your site\'s front end, below is an example of this:','wp-config file to restore from'=>'wp-config file to restore from','Restore from a backed up wp-config file'=>'Restore from a backed up wp-config file','Press the button below to backup and download the contents of the currently active wp-config.php file.'=>'Press the button below to backup and download the contents of the currently active wp-config.php file.','Save the current wp-config.php file'=>'Save the current wp-config.php file','You can also restore your site\'s wp-config.php settings using a backed up wp-config.php file.'=>'You can also restore your site\'s wp-config.php settings using a backed up wp-config.php file.','This feature allows you to backup and save your currently active wp-config.php file should you need to re-use the the backed up file in the future.'=>'This feature allows you to backup and save your currently active wp-config.php file should you need to re-use the the backed up file in the future.','wp-config.php file operations'=>'wp-config.php file operations','Your wp-config.php file has successfully been restored.'=>'Your wp-config.php file has successfully been restored.','Please choose a wp-config.php file to restore from.'=>'Please choose a wp-config.php file to restore from.','.htaccess file to restore from'=>'.htaccess file to restore from','Restore from a backed up .htaccess file'=>'Restore from a backed up .htaccess file','Press the button below to backup and save the currently active .htaccess file.'=>'Press the button below to backup and save the currently active .htaccess file.','Save the current .htaccess file'=>'Save the current .htaccess file','You can also restore your site\'s .htaccess settings using a backed up .htaccess file.'=>'You can also restore your site\'s .htaccess settings using a backed up .htaccess file.','This feature allows you to backup and save your currently active .htaccess file should you need to re-use the the backed up file in the future.'=>'This feature allows you to backup and save your currently active .htaccess file should you need to re-use the the backed up file in the future.','Your ".htaccess" file is a key component of your website\'s security and it can be modified to implement various levels of protection mechanisms.'=>'Your ".htaccess" file is a key component of your website\'s security and it can be modified to implement various levels of protection mechanisms.','.htaccess file operations'=>'.htaccess file operations','Your .htaccess file has successfully been restored.'=>'Your .htaccess file has successfully been restored.','Please choose a valid .htaccess to restore from.'=>'Please choose a valid .htaccess to restore from.','htaccess backup failed.'=>'htaccess backup failed.','All other bots from other organizations such as "Yahoo", "Bing" etc will not be affected by this feature.'=>'All other bots from other organisations such as "Yahoo", "Bing" etc will not be affected by this feature.','NOTE: If you use Jetpack or the Wordpress iOS or other apps then you should enable this feature but leave the "Completely Block Access To XMLRPC" checkbox unchecked.'=>'NOTE: If you use Jetpack or the WordPress iOS or other apps then you should enable this feature but leave the "Completely Block Access To XMLRPC" checkbox unchecked.','By leaving this feature enabled you will prevent Jetpack or Wordpress iOS or other apps which need XMLRPC from working correctly on your site.'=>'By leaving this feature enabled you will prevent Jetpack or WordPress iOS or other apps which need XMLRPC from working correctly on your site.','By enabling this checkbox, the plugin will add the necessary rules and exceptions so that AJAX operations will work as expected.'=>'By enabling this checkbox, the plugin will add the necessary rules and exceptions so that Ajax operations will work as expected.','In the cases where your WordPress installation has a theme or plugin that uses AJAX, a few extra lines of directives and exceptions need to be added to prevent AJAX requests from being automatically blocked by the brute force prevention feature.'=>'In the cases where your WordPress installation has a theme or plugin that uses Ajax, a few extra lines of directives and exceptions need to be added to prevent AJAX requests from being automatically blocked by the brute force prevention feature.','Enable this if your site uses AJAX functionality.'=>'Enable this if your site uses Ajax functionality.','My site has a theme or plugins which use AJAX'=>'My site has a theme or plugins which use Ajax','Press this button if you wish to download this log in CSV format.'=>'Press this button if you wish to download this log in CSV format.','Security strength meter'=>'Security strength meter','Permanently blocked IP addresses'=>'Permanently blocked IP addresses','NOTE: This feature does NOT use the .htaccess file to permanently block the IP addresses so it should be compatible with all web servers running WordPress.'=>'NOTE: This feature does NOT use the .htaccess file to permanently block the IP addresses so it should be compatible with all web servers running WordPress.','This tab displays the list of all permanently blocked IP addresses.'=>'This tab displays the list of all permanently blocked IP addresses.','Currently locked out IP addresses and ranges'=>'Currently locked out IP addresses and ranges','Permanent block list'=>'Permanent block list','Enable honeypot on login page'=>'Enable honeypot on login page','Login form honeypot settings'=>'Login form honeypot settings','Therefore, if the plugin detects that this field has a value when the form is submitted, then the robot which is attempting to submit the form on your site will be redirected to its localhost address - http://127.0.0.1.'=>'Therefore, if the plugin detects that this field has a value when the form is submitted, then the robot which is attempting to submit the form on your site will be redirected to its localhost address - http://127.0.0.1.','Since robots usually fill in every input field on a form, they will also submit a value for the special hidden honeypot field.'=>'Since robots usually fill in every input field on a form, they will also submit a value for the special hidden honeypot field.','To specify an IPv4 range use a wildcard "*" character, acceptable ways to use wildcards is shown in the examples below:'=>'To specify an IPv4 range use a wildcard "*" character, acceptable ways to use wildcards is shown in the examples below:','Enter whitelisted IP addresses:'=>'Enter whitelisted IP addresses:','You can copy and paste the above address(es) in the text box below if you want to include it in your login whitelist.'=>'You can copy and paste the above address(es) in the text box below if you want to include it in your login whitelist.','Your current IP address'=>'Your current IP address','Enable this if you want the whitelisting of selected IP addresses specified in the settings below'=>'Enable this if you want the whitelisting of selected IP addresses specified in the settings below','Enable IP whitelisting'=>'Enable IP whitelisting','Login IP whitelist settings'=>'Login IP whitelist settings','Attention: If in addition to enabling the white list feature, you also have one of the %1$s or %2$s features enabled, %3$s you will still need to use your secret word or special slug in the URL when trying to access your WordPress login page %4$s'=>'Attention: If in addition to enabling the white list feature, you also have one of the %1$s or %2$s features enabled, %3$s you will still need to use your secret word or special slug in the URL when trying to access your WordPress login page %4$s','By allowing/blocking IP addresses, you are using the most secure first line of defence because login access will only be granted to whitelisted IP addresses and other addresses will be blocked as soon as they try to access your login page.'=>'By allowing/blocking IP addresses, you are using the most secure first line of defence because login access will only be granted to whitelisted IP addresses and other addresses will be blocked as soon as they try to access your login page.','This feature will deny login access for all IP addresses which are not in your whitelist as configured in the settings below.'=>'This feature will deny login access for all IP addresses which are not in your whitelist as configured in the settings below.','The All-In-One Security Whitelist feature gives you the option of only allowing certain IP addresses or ranges to have access to your WordPress login page.'=>'The All-In-One Security Whitelist feature gives you the option of only allowing certain IP addresses or ranges to have access to your WordPress login page.','Enable CAPTCHA on WooCommerce registration form'=>'Enable CAPTCHA on WooCommerce registration form','Enable this if you want to insert CAPTCHA on a custom login form generated by the following WP function: %s'=>'Enable this if you want to insert CAPTCHA on a custom login form generated by the following WP function: %s','Enable this if you want to insert a CAPTCHA form on the lost password page.'=>'Enable this if you want to insert a CAPTCHA form on the lost password page.','Enable this if you want to insert a CAPTCHA form on the login page.'=>'Enable this if you want to insert a CAPTCHA form on the login page.','Secret key'=>'Secret key','Site key'=>'Site key','Adding a CAPTCHA form on a login page or form is another effective yet simple "Brute Force" prevention technique.'=>'Adding a CAPTCHA form on a login page or form is another effective yet simple "Brute Force" prevention technique.','This feature allows you to add a CAPTCHA form on various WordPress login pages and forms.'=>'This feature allows you to add a CAPTCHA form on various WordPress login pages and forms.','Perform cookie test'=>'Perform cookie test','Save feature settings'=>'Save feature settings','The cookie test was successful, you can now enable this feature.'=>'The cookie test was successful, you can now enable this feature.','If you do not use the WordPress password protection feature for your posts or pages then it is highly recommended that you leave this checkbox disabled.'=>'If you do not use the WordPress password protection feature for your posts or pages then it is highly recommended that you leave this checkbox disabled.','Helpful Tip:'=>'Helpful Tip:','By enabling this checkbox, the plugin will add the necessary rules and exceptions so that people trying to access these pages are not automatically blocked.'=>'By enabling this checkbox, the plugin will add the necessary rules and exceptions so that people trying to access these pages are not automatically blocked.','Normally if you wanted to login to WordPress you would type your site\'s home URL followed by wp-login.php.'=>'Normally if you wanted to login to WordPress you would type your site\'s home URL followed by wp-login.php.','There are also other ways Wordpress reveals version info such as during style and script loading, an example of this is:'=>'There are also other ways WordPress reveals version info such as during style and script loading, an example of this is:','Disallow unauthorized REST requests'=>'Disallow unauthorised REST requests','This feature allows you to block WordPress REST API access for unauthorized requests.'=>'This feature allows you to block WordPress REST API access for unauthorised requests.','Enable this if you want all visitors except those who are logged in as an administrator to be locked out of the front-end of your site.'=>'Enable this if you want all visitors except those who are logged in as an administrator to be locked out of the front end of your site.','Enable iFrame protection'=>'Enable iFrame protection','Unblock'=>'Unblock','Blocked IP'=>'Blocked IP','The selected user has been logged out successfully.'=>'The selected user has been logged out successfully.','Login name'=>'Login name','The selected IP address was unlocked successfully.'=>'The selected IP address was unlocked successfully.','The selected IP entries were unlocked successfully.'=>'The selected IP entries were unlocked successfully.','Unlock'=>'Unlock','Release date'=>'Release date','Date locked'=>'Date locked','Reason'=>'Reason','Locked IP/range'=>'Locked IP/range','Type'=>'Type','Message'=>'Message','Level'=>'Level','Date and time'=>'Date and time','Block'=>'Block','Status'=>'Status','Number of spam comments from this IP'=>'Number of spam comments from this IP','Spammer IP'=>'Spammer IP','User ID'=>'User ID','Delete'=>'Delete','Are you sure you want to delete this item?'=>'Are you sure you want to delete this item?','The selected IP addresses are now temporarily locked.'=>'The selected IP addresses are now temporarily locked.','Could not process the request because the IP addresses for the selected entries could not be found.'=>'Could not process the request because the IP addresses for the selected en